# CODEOWNERS — https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Rules are matched bottom-up: the LAST matching pattern wins, so the broad
# default comes first and the narrow overrides below it. Only the last match is
# used, not a union — putting a specific path above `*` does nothing.
#
# The default is the `maintainers` team, which exists and has `@TyperBody` as a
# maintainer. A reference to something that does not exist fails silently:
# GitHub requests nobody and the PR merely looks owned. Add people to the team
# rather than swapping the handle here.
#
# Every change needs a named reviewer from that team.

*                                   @E-SPower/maintainers

# Protocol v3, signing and the message field contract. A break here is expensive
# to undo, so it does not ride along in a larger PR unreviewed.
/backend/internal/protocol/         @E-SPower/maintainers
/backend/internal/messagefields/    @E-SPower/maintainers
/docs/developer-guide/protocol-v3.md @E-SPower/maintainers
/docs/developer-guide/message-fields.md @E-SPower/maintainers

# Platform registry: matrix.json generates public Go code and a public doc, so a
# matrix edit is a code change even when the diff is one JSON line.
/matrix.json                        @E-SPower/maintainers
/scripts/gen_platformspec.py        @E-SPower/maintainers
/scripts/gen_capabilities.py        @E-SPower/maintainers
/scripts/check_generated.py         @E-SPower/maintainers
/backend/internal/platformspec/     @E-SPower/maintainers

# The merge gate itself — workflows, template, labels, this file. A broken CI
# config is invisible until it is on `main`.
/.github/                           @E-SPower/maintainers

# Front end design tokens and the shared component library: a UI-SPEC violation
# is review feedback, not a nit.
/web/tailwind.config.js             @E-SPower/maintainers
/web/src/components/ui/             @E-SPower/maintainers
/web/UI-SPEC.md                     @E-SPower/maintainers

# Auth, secrets and the security policy.
/backend/internal/middleware/       @E-SPower/maintainers
/backend/internal/service/auth.go   @E-SPower/maintainers
/.github/SECURITY.md                @E-SPower/maintainers
